> Can you share more about the benchmark you added? Is it just calling `WriteFieldsDirective`?

Yes, since the main changes are on writing the directives in the stream. 
You can find below the benchmark code use to see the perf. I used a simple benchmark with all fields directive

```csharp
[ShortRunJob]
[MemoryDiagnoser]
public class BenchmarkW3CLogger
{
   var _path = Path.GetTempFileName() + "_";

    [Benchmark]
    public async Task WriteAllFieldDirective()
    {
        var options = new W3CLoggerOptions()
        {
            LoggingFields = W3CLoggingFields.All,
            LogDirectory = _path
        };

        await using (var processor = new W3CLoggerProcessor(new OptionsWrapperMonitor<W3CLoggerOptions>(options), new HostingEnvironment(), NullLoggerFactory.Instance))
        {
            await processor.WriteFieldsDirectiveBenchmark(StreamWriter.Null, CancellationToken.None);
        }
    }
}
```

